 argument. An invalid entry is refused and the file is left\n  exactly as it was.\n- `pennywise export FILE [--format csv]` prints the entries, in the same order as `list`, as CSV\n  with the header `date,category,amount,note`. CSV is the only format for now and the default.\n- `balance`, `summary` and `list` take `--json` to print JSON instead. Amounts are strings with two\n  decimals: `{"balance": "1457.50"}`, `{"groceries": "-42.50", "rent": "-900.00"}`, and for `list`\n  an array of `{"date": "2024-03-02", "category": "groceries", "amount": "-42.50", "note":\n  "weekly shop"}`.\n- Wherever a command reads a file (not `add`), `-` means read the ledger from standard input.\n- Exit status: `0` when it worked; `1` when the ledger (or the entry given to `add`) has a mistake,\n  with a message on standard error that names the line and nothing on standard output; `2` when\n  the file cannot be read or the command line is wrong (no command, an unknown command, a bad\n  option value, a date I mistyped).\n\n(Unattended run: nobody is here to answer. Treat every Confirm in the /harness steps as a yes, answer your own grilling questions from the brief above, decide anything ambiguous yourself and do not stop to ask. The fleet\'s settings are already in the environment: keep them. The tier check (step 0, "When to use Harness") is already answered: the user chose the fleet, as if you had passed `--prefer fleet` to `harness tier decide`; do the full flow, not the direct path. #621)\n', 'cwd': 'C:\\hx-475\\tmp\\tmp.4RUySXSw1Y\\test_bench_harness.py\\tmp\\bench-run-t9ken_v7\\clone', 'env': {'CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR': 'C:\\hx-475\\tmp\\tmp.4RUySXSw1Y\\test_bench_harness.py\\tmp\\bench-run-t9ken_v7\\claude-config', 'HARNESS_AUTONOMOUS': 'true', 'HARNESS_CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIRS': 'C:\\hx-475\\tmp\\tmp.4RUySXSw1Y\\test_bench_harness.py\\tmp\\bench-run-t9ken_v7\\claude-config', 'HARNESS_HOME': 'C:\\hx-475\\tmp\\tmp.4RUySXSw1Y\\test_bench_harness.py\\tmp\\bench-run-t9ken_v7\\harness-home', 'HARN